diff --git a/model/Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next/README.md b/model/Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next/README.md
index 3f6aad5..4dafa8e 100644
--- a/model/Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next/README.md
+++ b/model/Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next/README.md
@@ -32,6 +32,20 @@ MTP remains part of the text service. The model card selects the predictor param
 
 The vision presets acquire `mmproj-BF16.gguf` directly into the separate `vision` scope. They accept `image_url` and `video_url` parts interleaved with text, up to 768 supplied images/frames within the request and context budgets. Video uses vLLM-compatible JPEG sequences and request-wide frame timing, with the trained two-frame temporal projection; an odd tail aliases its final frame. The projector activates on demand and can release its weights while retained conversations keep their image-conditioned state. Text-only presets retain their original stage catalog and do not acquire or compile the projector. The [overview](OVERVIEW.md#image-conditioned-chat) includes a complete request.
 
+## PLE table: partial residency
+
+The 26.82 GiB `per_layer_token_embd.weight` table (IQ4_NL) is split into 16 hash heads of about 1.68 GiB, each a contiguous row range. The compile-time config `flash_next.ple_resident_heads` (K, 0 to 16) keeps the first K heads resident, bound as a prefix view of the table and looked up inside the epoch. The remaining heads are read on demand with `parameters.gather` (within-epoch dedupe and a 500 MiB GPU row cache). K = 0 binds no table rows; K = 16 is the catalog behavior (whole table resident, no gather).
+
+| Presets | K | Resident weights | Use when |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `chat`, `mtp`, `mtp-continuation`, `long-context`, `long-context-mtp`, `vision`, `vision-mtp` (default) | 0 | 77.2 GiB (80.2 GiB with MTP) | about 100 GiB of GTT, such as DevLab runners or a 128 GB box with other work running |
+| `chat-ple-k12`, `long-context-ple-k12`, `vision-ple-k12` (opt-in) | 12 | 97.3 GiB | partial residency, needs about 110 GiB of host memory, prefill 10 to 25 percent faster |
+| `mtp-ple-k10`, `mtp-continuation-ple-k10`, `long-context-mtp-ple-k10`, `vision-mtp-ple-k10` (opt-in) | 10 | 96.9 GiB | partial residency with MTP (fixed pool backing; K = 12 exceeds the box at about 107 GiB of GTT), needs about 110 GiB of host memory |
+
+Measured on a 128 GB box (rows 1, context 4096, prefill 2048): prefill of a 1,880-token prompt runs at 1041 tok/s with K = 0, 1157 with K = 8, 1252 with K = 12 and 1297 with K = 14; peak GTT 80, 94, 100 and 104 GiB.
+
+Every K produces identical greedy output. Other values of K can be set with the `flash_next.ple_resident_heads` key in a variant `config`.
+
 ## Build representations and regressions
 
 `source` and `archive` describe provider representations. A source package retains `.loom` files; an archive package contains `.loombc` providers for runtime linking. Both retain the explicit weight-preparation source as auxiliary compiler data. The programs share the same public service contracts and parameter identities.
